# ============================================================
# Unity generated folders (machine-local, never committed)
# ============================================================
# Anchored to the repository root. Unanchored, these match a directory of the same name at any
# depth: an Editor/Build/ folder had its .meta staged and none of its contents, with git reporting
# nothing. [Oo]bj/ stays unanchored because the .NET build writes one beside every csproj.
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
# Test-result XML from a hand-run sweep. The harnesses under scripts/ default to Logs/, already ignored
# above; this covers the directory a hand-run names instead, after nine such files reached a commit.
/merged/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/

# Recordings can get excessive in size. Anchored for the reason above.
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Asset meta data should only be ignored when the corresponding asset is also ignored
!/[Aa]ssets/**/*.meta

# The Unity Test Framework writes its PlayMode bootstrap scene here and deletes it when the run
# ends, so it sits in the working tree while a run is in flight and after one is killed. Below the
# re-include above: the last matching pattern wins, and placed before it the .meta stays untracked.
/[Aa]ssets/InitTestScene*

# ============================================================
# IDE / build tool artifacts
# ============================================================
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
# Unity regenerates these at the project root. Anchored so the hand-authored projects
# under Generators~ and docs/ stay committed — an unanchored rule drops a new one
# silently and only fails on a fresh clone.
/*.csproj
/*.sln
*.user
*.userprefs
*.unityproj
*.suo
*.tmp
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db
ExportedObj/
.consulo/
.vsconfig

# Unity3D generated meta files
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# ============================================================
# OS / misc
# ============================================================
.DS_Store
crashlytics-build.properties

# Unity license / activation files — never commit (they carry machine bindings, device serial, hostname)
*.ulf
*.alf

# ============================================================
# Build outputs / packaged artifacts
# ============================================================
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app

# ============================================================
# Source-generator build intermediates (Velvet Generators~)
# Committed artifacts live under Runtime/Plugins; bin/obj are not committed.
# ============================================================
**/Generators~/**/bin/
**/Generators~/**/obj/

# ============================================================
# DocFX generated output (docs site is built by CI, not committed)
# ============================================================
docs/api/
docs/_site/
docs/obj/
docs/bin/
# Disposable build-time copy of Packages/com.velvet.core/Documentation~ staged by docs/build.py
# so DocFX's TOC/xref resolution can see the guides; Documentation~ remains the single source.
docs/guides/
# The hand-authored DocFX and source-generator projects need no re-include: the *.csproj / *.sln rules
# above are anchored to the root, so no rule ever matched them. Four negations sat here saying otherwise
# and reached nothing.

# Written by com.unity.settings-manager the first time a package that uses it loads. The one the
# Code Coverage package leaves holds an empty dictionary, and CI passes its coverage options on the
# command line rather than reading this, so tracking it would only make every checkout dirty after
# its first run.
ProjectSettings/Packages/

# Python bytecode, written beside a hook by anything that imports it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# pytest's cache root, written by running the scripts/ suites through pytest rather than unittest.
/.pytest_cache/
